## Adjudication

### 1. Fidelity to Decision 5 — PASS

- dht-scheme is plain data, byte-identical to the design's descriptor
  (host/gambit/yin/jolt/gambit/yin.jolt:11-15). The only new require is
  dao.posix.file (:4), which itself requires only jolt.scheme — no
  yin.shell.dht, no dao.stream.udp, no java.io.File anywhere on the load path.
- Startup :parse-store-arg is unchanged (yin.jolt:44-49, wired at :71);
  yin.repl.main consumes :parse-store-command only in swap_store
  (main.cljc:497) and parses startup flags solely via :parse-store-arg
  (main.cljc:185,226), so --index-store file:/dht: still refuses startup with
  exit 1 (parse-store + store/parse-arg without extra schemes → "Unknown
  --index-store").
- open-gambit (yin.jolt:38-42) evaluates (posix-file/realpath (:dir spec)) as
  the FIRST expression on the non-mem path; {:index-store (store/open spec)}
  is unreachable behind it because realpath unconditionally routes to
  joltffi-public-blocking-raise (host/gambit/yin/dao/posix/file.jolt:20). The
  composed branch of replace-store calls the composition :open directly
  (main.cljc:456-457) without checked-spec, so no java.io.File and no spec-type
  refusal can precede the C4 error.
- :mem path delegates to open-memory (yin.jolt:33-36), preserving
  :engine-inputs {:host-modules {jolt.ffi …, dao.jing.mem …}} — proven by the
  transcript's post-swap (require 'jolt.ffi) → 'jolt.ffi and
  (jolt.ffi/sizeof :int32) → 4.
- :composition-spec? (constantly true): exactly two consumers — boot
  (main.cljc:288-291) and replace-store (main.cljc:453). At boot only :mem can
  reach it (parse-store gates earlier), so behavior is identical to the old
  #{:mem}; at swap, always-composed is correct on Gambit because open-gambit
  self-dispatches :mem vs durable. No other composition key is affected:
  admitting?/refusal/step/startup-lines/banner-lines are absent → engine
  defaults (composition-admitting? true, no transport step), so quiesce,
  reset, evaluation, and shutdown paths are un-hijacked. Non-swap behavior is
  unchanged (old map was a subset of the new one).

### 2. parse-swap-command contract — PASS (one LOW)

- Grammar parity with the design and with the reference
  yin.shell.cli/parse-store-command (cli.cljc:608-639): identical supported
  text ("mem, file:<dir>, dht:<dir>"), identical no-args / bad-target /
  options-must-be-keyword-value-pairs messages, and the exact design string
  "store options require dht:<dir>" for trailing opts on :mem/:file.
  :mem is normalized to "mem" (label matches swap-summary's output).
- Driver feeding is correct: driver.cljc:447 passes
  (rest (adapter/command-form line)) — a seq of forms matching the
  [[target & options :as args]] destructure.
- main.cljc:503's describe-spec guard is correctly skipped when the
  composition supplies its own parser (dht: specs must pass through).
- LOW (below): the return map omits the contract's :opts key.

### 3. Transcript state machine — PASS

- All 20 replies are asserted in order with step gating; any extra yin> line
  fails via the catch-all. The C4 rules (steps 9/13/14) are unanchored
  prefixes, matching the full message including the "— GC-safe blocking is
  unqualified on Gambit 4.9.8 (no verified release/claim transition)" tail.
  The quiesce rule (step 10) is fully anchored and matches
  yin.repl/swap-refusal's exact string (repl.cljc:2540). Step 15's "Switched
  index store to mem (code index cleared)" matches swap-summary (label "mem",
  :mem spec → "(code index cleared)", repl.cljc:2579-2587).
- Decision 5's failure story is fully covered: dirty swap refused (step 10),
  state survives ((+ p1c-score 1) → 101, step 11 — this IS design story step
  2's (+ x 1) survival probe), reset (12), C4 for file: (13), C4 for dht:
  (14), mem swap succeeds (15), post-swap evaluation (16-18), clean exit 0
  (19 + watchdog status check).
- Deviation 1 (require 'jolt.ffi before the post-swap sizeof): necessary and
  precedented. A swap rebuilds the VM session (make-session → make-vm) with a
  clean symbol environment while :host-modules repopulates the registry, so
  guest code must require to link — exactly the pattern the pre-swap sequence
  in the same script already uses (FORMS lines 20-21) and the pattern
  documented in test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc ("a (reset) drops host modules:
  require the DHT one each time"). It strengthens the assertion: the require
  succeeding is itself proof that :host-modules survived the swap. ACCEPTED.
- Deviation 2 (the (+ p1c-score 1) → 101 probe): implements the design's
  failure-story step 2 verbatim rather than deviating from it. ACCEPTED.

### 4. Defect hunt — CLEAN

- No double-open/double-close on the mem path: one open per swap
  (open-gambit → open-memory → store/open); the old store is closed exactly
  once, after the commit point (main.cljc:481-482, release-store! with
  store/close! fallback since the Gambit composition has no :close-store!);
  an open-time throw (the C4 case) precedes both release calls and leaves the
  old store live; a failed install releases only the new store
  (main.cljc:478-480).
- No error swallowing around the C4 refusal: the new yin.jolt code contains
  no try/catch at all; swap_store's catch is
  #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) (main.cljc:506), which
  catches the host UnsupportedOperationException (ex-data nil) and formats it
  via format-swap-error — transcript-proven ("Error: blocking ffi is
  unsupported on the gambit target — …" printed inline, session survives).
  release-store! swallows only cleanup errors on retired/failed stores, which
  Decision 2 step 5 explicitly sanctions.
- The C4 boundary is unweakened: dao.posix.file's overlay is untouched (every
  function refuses), no blocking FFI is qualified or shimmed, and realpath is
  invoked for its refusal, not its effect. The refusal is not blocked-FFI
  qualified anywhere.
- Post-swap session is quiesced (make-session ends :quiesced? true,
  repl.cljc:1016; install-store rebuilds through it), so a subsequent swap is
  not wrongly refused.
- /tmp/gambit-nope is never created (all file ops refuse), and even a
  pre-existing directory would not change realpath's unconditional refusal.

